#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114976 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e970fe-cff8-50e3-9b94-67ad97b03da7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Power of a Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "f832e671-b4bd-5d1d-81e7-b215a8ee4e27" :question/math-academy-id "e-4414" :question/problem "Find $A^4$ given that $[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "First, to find $A^2,$ we multiply $A$ by itself:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2} & =A\\cdot A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 10 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $A^4 = A^2 \\cdot A^2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{4} & ={A}^{2}\\cdot {A}^{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 10 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 10 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}81 & 0 \\\\ 100 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114977 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "61443225-bc08-5d36-a603-3a1d7e392a98" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Matrix Polynomial"}] :question/id #uuid "bea8819f-6feb-5de6-a585-4379378ccdbd" :question/math-academy-id "e-4417" :question/problem "Consider the matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind $f(D)$ if $f(X)=-X^2+3X+2.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & =-{X}^{2}+3X+2 \\\\  & =-{X}^{2}+3X+2I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(D)=-D^2+3D+2I.$\n\nLet's calculate $D^2$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}^{2} & =D\\cdot D \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(D)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(D) & =-{D}^{2}+3D+2I \\\\  & =-[\\begin{aligned}1 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]+3[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]+2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -9\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 & 15 \\\\ 0 & -9\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1+3+2 & 10+15+0 \\\\ 0 & -9-9+2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 25 \\\\ 0 & -16\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284445 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e970fe-cff8-50e3-9b94-67ad97b03da7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Power of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f946525-3e2d-5abf-8f4f-ade88c6a78e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 12 \\\\ 14 & 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284447} {:answer/id #uuid "983c14d0-0db6-5203-bfe1-99c5b48dca63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284448} {:answer/id #uuid "698b32d9-6289-5b45-bcdc-a2c9e01f4e22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 12 \\\\ 4 & 19\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284449} {:answer/id #uuid "d9055baf-fb78-52f6-87c5-7fa9a4f63ffc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 & 12 \\\\ 1 & 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284450} {:answer/id #uuid "3596a79d-183e-540f-9d7a-11e50b3beb07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 12 \\\\ 4 & 19\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284451}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3596a79d-183e-540f-9d7a-11e50b3beb07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 12 \\\\ 4 & 19\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284451} :answer-field/id #uuid "a62ee48d-d3b9-5811-